Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:30:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] correlation groups: noise_model=both (default): the detector
 run with the analytic noise and with the bootstrap, groups combined

The two noise models rank pairs differently: the bootstrap over reflections discounts
correlations that rest on a few strong reflections (two crystals of one population sharing a
handful of strong spots), the analytic error does not, while the analytic error is the better
calibrated of the two where pairs share few reflections. Each finds groups the other misses;
combine_groups (tested) reports the groups found with the analytic noise and adds those found
with the bootstrap that share no data set with them.
---
 src/dials/algorithms/correlation/analysis.py | 56 +++++++++++++-------
 src/dials/algorithms/correlation/groups.py   | 23 ++++++++
 tests/algorithms/correlation/test_groups.py  | 13 +++++
 3 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

